{
  "_doc": "Selection cases shared by every Markdown source-map engine. 'selected' is the rendered text the user selects (soft line breaks read as a space). 'prefix' and 'suffix' are rendered text before and after it inside the same block (at most 40 characters). A 'resolved' case expects the tightest source slice containing the selected characters: markup delimiters are included only when they sit between selected characters, never at the edges. Ranges are half-open [start, end), given both in UTF-8 bytes and UTF-16 code units because the unit is decided by the F1 spike (decision 0005). An 'ambiguous' case expects the engine to flag it, never to pick a match; 'candidates' is how many places the selection and context match. 'heading_path' is null when the matches sit under different headings. Files listed in 'hostile_files' must render with no script, event-handler attribute or javascript: link.",
  "hostile_files": [
    "hostile.md"
  ],
